+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry owns validation of model-supplied arguments against the same JSON Schema exposed to providers, so executors can rely on the declared input contract.
+
+## Contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` checks required fields, declared types and enums before execution, returns a descriptive `ToolResponse` on rejection without invoking the executor, names failing property paths and constraints in results and logs without exposing input values, passes valid input including unknown keys unchanged exactly once without coercion or defaults, and preserves the unknown-tool exception ([validated by: rejects malformed input privately and passes valid input unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L30)).
+- Static schemas compile at registration, fail there with the tool name if invalid, and reuse the compiled validation across subsequent executions ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and reuses them for ten calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L101)).
+- Function-valued definitions resolve at execution time, validate against the current schema, and cache compilation by resolved schema object identity ([validated by: validates each dynamic definition and caches by schema identity](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L119)).
+
+## Integration and delivery
+
+A rejected input is a normal tool result available to the model for a corrected retry within the existing five-round bound; executor failures are not input validation failures and retain their existing behavior.
+
+The implementation uses a JSON Schema validator in runtime dependencies, with no opt-out flag; documentation in README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md and .specify/spec.md must explain rejection results, unchanged extra keys and the tool-round retry bound, and execute carries a one-line comment linking here.
+
+Release delivery includes an npm-facing CHANGELOG entry, a MINOR version bump, and a PR migration note explaining that executors no longer see malformed input to produce their own validation errors; package build, import and repository CI checks remain required.
